@base = http://127.0.0.1:8080/api
# Change these three to ids that exist in your database (the screens do not show ids; the GET requests below do).
@itemId = 1
@netRateItemId = 2
@partyId = 1

### 1. First-run setup (fresh database)
POST {{base}}/setup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "shopName": "Chirag Auto Parts",
  "cashBillPrefix": "C-", "partyBillPrefix": "P-",
  "voucherPrefix": "PV-", "supplierPaymentPrefix": "SP-",
  "startingBillNumber": 1001,
  "openingCashInHand": 5000.00, "openingCashInHandDate": "2026-04-01",
  "printShowShopName": true, "printShowAddress": true, "printShowPhone": true,
  "printShowLogo": true, "printShowThankyou": true, "printShowMrp": true
}

### 2. Bill top line: save one -> topLine comes back
PUT {{base}}/shop-profile
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "shopName": "Chirag Auto Parts",
  "cashBillPrefix": "C-", "partyBillPrefix": "P-",
  "voucherPrefix": "PV-", "supplierPaymentPrefix": "SP-",
  "startingBillNumber": 1001,
  "openingCashInHand": 5000.00, "openingCashInHandDate": "2026-04-01",
  "printShowShopName": true, "printShowAddress": true, "printShowPhone": true,
  "printShowLogo": true, "printShowThankyou": true, "printShowMrp": true,
  "topLine": "Shree Ganeshaya Namah"
}

### 3. Blank top line -> topLine null
PUT {{base}}/shop-profile
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "shopName": "Chirag Auto Parts",
  "cashBillPrefix": "C-", "partyBillPrefix": "P-",
  "voucherPrefix": "PV-", "supplierPaymentPrefix": "SP-",
  "startingBillNumber": 1001,
  "openingCashInHand": 5000.00, "openingCashInHandDate": "2026-04-01",
  "printShowShopName": true, "printShowAddress": true, "printShowPhone": true,
  "printShowLogo": true, "printShowThankyou": true, "printShowMrp": true,
  "topLine": "   "
}

### 4. Two parties
POST {{base}}/parties
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Search Party", "phone": "9822011223", "city": "Kolhapur", "openingBalance": 300.00 }

###
POST {{base}}/parties
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Advance Party", "openingBalance": -100.00 }

### 5. Search by city text, then by phone digits -> one party each
GET {{base}}/parties?q=kolhap

###
GET {{base}}/parties?q=822011

### 6. Party summary -> totalParties 2, partiesWithBalance 2, totalOutstanding 300.00, totalAdvance 100.00
GET {{base}}/parties/summary

### 7. A supplier and a search by city
# @name supplier
POST {{base}}/suppliers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Hero Depot", "phone": "9822077889", "city": "Pune" }

###
GET {{base}}/suppliers?q=pune

### 8. A supplier payment (cash 250.00)
POST {{base}}/supplier-payments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "supplierId": {{supplier.response.body.id}}, "paymentDate": "2026-11-01", "amount": 250.00, "paymentMode": "CASH" }

### 9. Supplier summary -> totalSuppliers 1, paymentCount 1, paymentTotal 250.00, cashInHand 4750.00
GET {{base}}/suppliers/summary

### 10. Dashboard -> kpis.cashInHand 4750.00 (the same figure)
GET {{base}}/dashboard?period=TODAY

### 11. One supplier -> paymentCount 1, paymentTotal 250.00
GET {{base}}/suppliers/{{supplier.response.body.id}}/summary

### 12. Unknown supplier -> 404 NOT_FOUND
GET {{base}}/suppliers/999999/summary

### 13. Upload the shop logo (put a real path after the <)
# The same call with curl in PowerShell:
#   curl.exe -i -F "file=@C:\path\to\logo.png" http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/shop-profile/logo
# Refusals, each answers 400 with field "file":
#   Set-Content -Path "$env:TEMP\notes.png" -Value "not an image"
#   [IO.File]::WriteAllBytes("$env:TEMP\big.png", (New-Object byte[] 3000000))
#   curl.exe -i -F "file=@$env:TEMP\notes.png" http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/shop-profile/logo   (Only PNG or JPEG images are accepted.)
#   curl.exe -i -F "file=@$env:TEMP\big.png" http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/shop-profile/logo     (The image is larger than 2 MB.)
#   curl.exe -i -F "other=x" http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/shop-profile/logo                     (Choose an image file to upload.)
POST {{base}}/shop-profile/logo
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=VIRABOUNDARY

--VIRABOUNDARY
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="logo.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< C:/path/to/logo.png
--VIRABOUNDARY--

### 14. Read the logo back -> the image, Cache-Control: no-cache
GET {{base}}/shop-profile/logo

### 15. Remove the logo -> 204, then request 14 answers 404 NOT_FOUND
DELETE {{base}}/shop-profile/logo

### 16. A saved Cash discount locks the item's Item Type (@itemId is an MRP item) -> source CASH_OVERRIDE
POST {{base}}/pricing/permanent-changes
Content-Type: application/json

{ "itemId": {{itemId}}, "customer": "CASH", "field": "DISCOUNT_PERCENT", "newValue": 12 }

### 17. A saved Party discount (MRP item) and a saved Party net rate (Net Rate item) -> both appear on the party's Item Rates tab
POST {{base}}/pricing/permanent-changes
Content-Type: application/json

{ "itemId": {{itemId}}, "customer": "PARTY", "partyId": {{partyId}}, "field": "DISCOUNT_PERCENT", "newValue": 8 }

###
POST {{base}}/pricing/permanent-changes
Content-Type: application/json

{ "itemId": {{netRateItemId}}, "customer": "PARTY", "partyId": {{partyId}}, "field": "NET_RATE", "newValue": 110 }

### 18. How many saved rates does the item have? (the count the Items screen shows)
GET {{base}}/items/{{itemId}}/rate-overrides

### 19. Remove every saved rate -> 204; the Item Type can be changed again
DELETE {{base}}/items/{{itemId}}/rate-overrides

### 20. Recalculate Balances: first break two stored figures in MySQL (not here), then list the mismatches
# UPDATE party SET current_balance = current_balance + 10 WHERE id = 1;   -- use the @partyId value
# UPDATE cash_in_hand SET balance = balance + 5 WHERE id = 1;
GET {{base}}/maintenance/recalculate-balances

### 21. Correct the stored cash, then that party (what the Correct buttons on Settings do)
POST {{base}}/maintenance/recalculate-balances/cash

###
POST {{base}}/maintenance/recalculate-balances/parties/{{partyId}}

### 22. After the corrections every figure matches
GET {{base}}/maintenance/recalculate-balances

### 23. The figures behind the Selected Party tiles (V23)
GET {{base}}/parties/{{partyId}}/balance-summary

###
GET {{base}}/daybook?partyId={{partyId}}&size=1

###
GET {{base}}/payment-vouchers?partyId={{partyId}}&size=1